{"id":"n-20261021-6nfvx4","category":"world","display_title":"US Importer Sues Trump Administration Over Canadian Tariffs","display_title_he":"יבואן אמריקאי תובע את ממשל טראמפ בשל מכסים על קנדה","short_summary":"A major US food importer has filed a lawsuit challenging President Trump's 50% tariffs on Canadian goods, claiming the administration exceeded its legal authority.","english_level":"C1","words":486,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"BBC News","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqrkyj13m588o","title":"Trump sued over Canadian tariffs in latest legal challenge","published_at":"2026-10-20T19:30:05.000Z"},{"name":"CNBC","domain":"cnbc.com","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/20/trump-tariffs-canada-section-338-lawsuit.html","title":"Trump sued over 50% tariffs on Canada in latest trade challenge","published_at":"2026-10-20T18:06:13.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-20T18:06:13.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-21T06:10:02.530Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["A major legal battle has erupted in the United States Court of International Trade as a family-owned food importer challenges President Donald Trump’s decision to slap sweeping 50 percent tariffs on an extensive array of Canadian goods. The lawsuit, filed on Tuesday by the Liberty Justice Center on behalf of New Jersey-based Gellert Global Group, marks the latest constitutional and statutory clash over executive authority in American trade policy. The dispute centers on the White House’s unprecedented invocation of Section 338 of the Tariff Act of 1930—a nearly century-old Depression-era statute aimed at combating foreign trade discrimination—to impose duties on products ranging from specialty cheeses and wine to honey, wigs, and hockey sticks.","The trade measures were initially promulgated in July through presidential proclamations after bilateral trade negotiations between Washington and Ottawa collapsed. The administration justified the levies by alleging that Canadian regulations unfairly disadvantaged American motor vehicles, dairy, and alcohol sectors. However, the new complaint asserts that the administration exceeded its constitutional mandate and failed to establish a legitimate legal foundation. According to the lawsuit, Canadian policy measures cited by the White House do not constitute discrimination; rather, they represent lawful countermeasures against prior American tariffs or reflect agreed-upon terms under the United States-Mexico-Canada Agreement (USMCA). Furthermore, the legal advocacy group contends that Section 338 was impliedly repealed by Section 301 of the Trade Act of 1974, and that administration officials violated procedural mandates by failing to observe a required 30-day waiting period before collecting the levies.","For Gellert Global Group, a third-generation business generating over $1.7 billion in annual revenue, the financial ramifications are severe. Having imported $71 million worth of Canadian cheeses—including mascarpone, brie, and camembert—duty-free in 2025 under USMCA provisions, the firm now faces an estimated annual tariff burden of $40 million. Co-chief executive Thomas Gellert emphasized that these sudden levies disrupt long-standing commercial relationships throughout the supply chain. Although the firm intends to absorb costs temporarily through the end of the year, executives warned that prolonged duties will force steep price increases for consumers, imperil retail placements, and endanger suppliers. Compounding the burden, the company also faces retaliatory tariffs on its exports north of the border imposed by Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney, who matched the American levies dollar for dollar.","This action marks the fourth legal challenge brought by the Liberty Justice Center against the administration's tariff agenda. The public interest legal organization previously scored a landmark victory when the Supreme Court invalidated tariffs imposed under the International Emergency Economic Powers Act, prompting an ongoing government reimbursement process of approximately $166 billion to affected importers. Liberty Justice Center Chief Executive Sara Albrecht reiterated that the United States Constitution explicitly delegates tariff-setting authority to Congress rather than the executive branch, arguing that officials cannot simply shift policies between statutes. Motioning for a preliminary injunction, the lawsuit asks the trade court to declare the Canadian duties unlawful, halt enforcement immediately, and mandate full refunds with interest for impacted businesses."],"facts":[{"fact":"A family-owned food importer, Gellert Global Group, filed a lawsuit in the US Court of International Trade against President Trump's 50% tariffs on Canadian goods.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The Liberty Justice Center is representing Gellert Global Group in challenging the White House's use of Section 338 of the Tariff Act of 1930.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Trump invoked Section 338 in July following the breakdown of trade negotiations, applying tariffs to products such as cheese, wine, honey, wigs, and hockey sticks.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Gellert Global Group imported $71 million of Canadian cheese duty-free in 2025 under USMCA and faces an estimated $40 million annual tariff cost under the new rules.","sources":[2]},{"fact":"Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney retaliated with dollar-for-dollar tariffs on US goods, affecting Gellert's exports of American cheese to Canada.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The lawsuit argues Section 338 was superseded by Section 301 of the Trade Act of 1974 and that the administration failed to observe a required 30-day waiting period.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"This is the Liberty Justice Center's fourth lawsuit against Trump's tariffs, following a Supreme Court decision invalidating duties under the IEEPA that led to $166 billion in refunds.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"major","lemma":"major","pos":"adjective","he":"מרכזי, משמעותי","name":false},{"text":"legal battle","lemma":"legal battle","pos":"compound","he":"מאבק משפטי","name":false},{"text":"erupted","lemma":"erupt","pos":"verb","he":"פרץ","name":false},{"text":"United States Court of International Trade","lemma":"United States Court of International Trade","pos":"name","he":"בית המשפט של ארה\"ב לסחר בינלאומי","name":true},{"text":"family-owned","lemma":"family-owned","pos":"adjective","he":"בבעלות משפחתית","name":false},{"text":"food importer","lemma":"food importer","pos":"compound","he":"יבואן מזון","name":false},{"text":"challenges","lemma":"challenge","pos":"verb","he":"מאתגר, מגיש ערעור נגד","name":false},{"text":"President Donald Trump","lemma":"President Donald Trump","pos":"name","he":"הנשיא דונלד טראמפ","name":true},{"text":"decision","lemma":"decision","pos":"noun","he":"החלטה","name":false},{"text":"slap","lemma":"slap","pos":"verb","he":"להטיל (מכסים בקלות דעת או בחומרה)","name":false},{"text":"sweeping","lemma":"sweeping","pos":"adjective","he":"גורף, נרחב","name":false},{"text":"percent","lemma":"percent","pos":"noun","he":"אחוז","name":false},{"text":"tariffs","lemma":"tariff","pos":"noun","he":"מכסים","name":false},{"text":"extensive","lemma":"extensive","pos":"adjective","he":"נרחב","name":false},{"text":"array","lemma":"array","pos":"noun","he":"מגוון, שורה","name":false},{"text":"Canadian","lemma":"Canadian","pos":"adjective","he":"קנדי","name":false},{"text":"goods","lemma":"goods","pos":"noun","he":"סחורות, טובין","name":false},{"text":"lawsuit","lemma":"lawsuit","pos":"noun","he":"תביעה משפטית","name":false},{"text":"filed","lemma":"file","pos":"verb","he":"הוגשה","name":false},{"text":"Tuesday","lemma":"Tuesday","pos":"name","he":"יום שלישי","name":true},{"text":"Liberty Justice Center","lemma":"Liberty Justice Center","pos":"name","he":"מרכז החרות והצדק","name":true},{"text":"on behalf of","lemma":"on